codex
The first symbolic run exposed two spurious branches caused by overly broad framed maps: the prover had to consider a module scope shadowing `len` with a closure cell and unrelated heap objects. Those states are not reachable from this invocation, so I’m narrowing the invariant to the exact module binding and one accumulator heap object; this is a theorem-strengthening repair, not a semantic shortcut.
apply patch
patch: completed
/workspace/spec.k
diff --git a/smoke.py b/smoke.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9e6de560c209cefef0b5e69f621ed6b130913378
--- /dev/null
+++ b/smoke.py
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+def sorted_list_sum(lst):
+    result = []
+    word = ""
+    for word in lst:
+        if len(word) % 2 == 0:
+            result.append(word)
+    return sorted(sorted(result), key=len)
+
+
+assert sorted_list_sum([]) == []
+assert sorted_list_sum(["aa", "a", "aaa"]) == ["aa"]
+assert sorted_list_sum(["ab", "a", "aaa", "cd"]) == ["ab", "cd"]
+assert sorted_list_sum(
+    ["zz", "b", "aa", "cccc", "bb", "ddd", "aa"]
+) == ["aa", "aa", "bb", "zz", "cccc"]
+assert sorted_list_sum(["x", "yyy"]) == []
